{:adr-id "2607154000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-0145 (raising of swine/pigs) swine-farm-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607152100" "ADR-2607122200" "ADR-2607011000"]

 :context
 "cloud-itonami-isic-0144 did not exist prior to this ADR (verified via gh repo view
  before starting -- no failed prior attempt to recover from). The task assignment
  specified ISIC class 0144 for swine/pigs, but this numeric code was incorrect: per
  the authoritative kotoba-lang/industry registry (matching the real UN ISIC Rev.4
  standard), 0144 is 'Raising of sheep and goats' and 0145 is 'Raising of swine/pigs'.
  Discovered mid-build by reading the registry's 0141/0144/0145 entries side by side
  before the registry-edit step. Rather than write incorrect data into the shared
  registry (labeling 0144, sheep/goats, as :implemented with swine content), the
  GitHub repo was renamed cloud-itonami-isic-0144 -> cloud-itonami-isic-0145
  (redirect preserved), all in-repo ISIC-code references corrected, and the fix
  committed/pushed/re-verified BEFORE any registry work touched kotoba-lang/industry.
  The registry's own 0144 (sheep/goats) entry is untouched -- a distinct, unrelated
  ISIC class left for future coverage. Built from cloud-itonami-isic-0141 (raising
  of cattle and buffaloes) as the module-structure template, with clojure -M:test
  independently re-run before and after every push."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct animal handling (farm operator's exclusive authority)"
  "veterinary treatment decisions (veterinarian/farm operator authority)"
  "slaughter or culling decisions (economic and ethical authority remains human)"
  "disease-outbreak declarations / animal-health authority contact (actor only
    surfaces a flagged concern for human/veterinary judgment)"
  "ISIC 0144 (Raising of sheep and goats) itself -- a separate, unrelated ISIC
    class, out of scope for this ADR"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-0145 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Advisor,
  Phase, Operation, Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-0141 module-for-module, adapted
  from cattle-ranching to swine-farming -- barn/pen management instead of pasture,
  biosecurity concepts like ASF instead of generic disease):
  - Governor (SwineFarmOperationsGovernor): 5 hard checks (facility-not-registered,
    no-execution, treatment-or-slaughter-blocked, op-not-allowed, herd-count-invalid)
    + 3 escalation gates (always-escalate health/biosecurity concern, cost-threshold
    supply orders, low confidence < 0.7)
  - Facts: supply categories with cost thresholds (feed/veterinary-supply/
    biosecurity-equipment), breeds (landrace/duroc/yorkshire/berkshire), and a
    biosecurity/notifiable-disease reference vocabulary (ASF/CSF/FMD/PRRS) -- purely
    descriptive, never changes the Governor's disposition
  - Registry: independent pure predicates (cost-exceeds-threshold?,
    herd-count-non-positive?, confidence-below-floor?)
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (registered-facility lookup)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + MockAdvisor (4 ops)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate
  - Operation: composes advisor -> governor -> phase-gate (langgraph-clj wiring
    deferred, matching 0141's own stub)
  - Sim: demo runner with a working -main
  - Operations: log-herd-record (herd count/weight/health-check/farrowing data),
    schedule-veterinary-visit, flag-animal-health-concern (ALWAYS escalates, e.g.
    suspected ASF), order-supplies (closed allowlist, :effect :propose)
  - Tests: 31 tests / 99 assertions (facts, governor, phase, registry, store), all
    green
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - GitHub repo created as cloud-itonami-isic-0144, renamed to cloud-itonami-isic-0145
    once the code mislabel was caught, before any registry work"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["Swine-raising (0145) now genuinely implemented and fully tested"
   "0144/0145 code mislabel caught before it could corrupt the shared
    kotoba-lang/industry registry -- 0144 (sheep/goats) entry untouched, 0145
    (swine/pigs) now correctly points at the real, tested actor repo"
   "Scope boundaries (animal handling, treatment, slaughter/culling) hardcoded in
    governor checks, not just asserted in prose"
   "Animal-health/biosecurity escalation (flag-animal-health-concern always human,
    e.g. suspected ASF) is a core design invariant; actor structurally cannot
    declare an outbreak or contact authorities itself"
   "Portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["Real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up (in-memory for now)"
   "langgraph-clj StateGraph wiring (real interrupt-before/checkpoint resume) is
    deferred scaffolding, matching 0141's own stub status"
   "ISIC 0144 (Raising of sheep and goats) remains unimplemented (:spec,
    gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0144 placeholder) -- a different ISIC class, left for a
    future agent/ADR"]}

